'''Stone Cat''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] added in [[Version 10.2 Update|Version 10.2]] who can be unlocked when beating the [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stage]] [[Possessed by Evil (Merciless)|Prelude to Ruin]] appearing on the '''11th''', '''12th''', '''25th''', and '''26th''' of every month.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 581
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Stone Cat
|name2 = Boulder Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Boulder Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Stone Cat has very high health for its cost but despawns moments after executing its attack. It is optimal for holding meatshield line in that half a second when a powerful enemy unleashes an attack, such as [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent bosses]] with [[Omni Strike]] like [[Daboo of the Dead|Daboo]] and [[Masked Okame]] or [[:Category:Surge Attack Enemies|Surge]] enemies like [[Lord of Ruin Jagando]], [[Kappy Jr.]] or [[St. Dober]] to delay their advance. This emergency line of defense is also usable on [[CyberFace]], [[Brollow]]s, and most other slow-attacking or hard-hitting enemies, or even a heavily buffed Gauntlet Colossus if given the chance.

Due to its short attack animation, Stone Cat won't stick around for more than the minimum time, though its immunities are effective in preventing it from being destroyed or delayed before reaching the frontlines. Like [[Capsule Cat (Special Cat)|Capsule Cat]], he can also be used for starting certain enemies' attack animations; this is useful against ranged foes such as [[THE SLOTH]] or [[Director Kurosawah]] to waste their attack, allowing you to send other units to cripple them.

Stone Cat's usage can also be drastically improved with Research Up [[Cat Combo]]s like [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]], [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]], [[Cheating Heart? (Combo)|Cheating Heart]], [[Kimono Champs (Combo)|Kimono Champs]] and [[Bad Guys (Combo)|Bad Guys]], with a recharge time more similar to some of your anti-trait specialist [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]] like [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] or [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], offering universal defense with far greater potential when your meatshields just wouldn't cut it, if not completely demolished by the enemy composition. This cat is also ideal for taking out isolated, low-magnification [[Assassin Bear]]s, as it has a massive amount of health, high speed and only one knockback, whilst dealing just enough damage to kill them immediately.

